WEBVTT

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.450
So he has everything?

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:09.070
Yes, Mythos was faster at securing 
admin access than we were.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.900
It seems Unit 8 didn't stop him in time 
because the USDF interfered.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.660
The USDF systems were taken over by Logos.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.030
It's MIAC's responsibility for not 
immediately reporting the compromise!

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:22.960
Now, stop. This is hardly the 
time to play the blame game.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.810
The greater problem is that

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.830
even our civilian systems have been taken over.

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:33.260
This is the reason so many devices have been 
hijacked by admin privilege overrides.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.520
The freeware, Liko.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.220
As you all know,

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.760
it's a popular app than can be 
installed on any computer.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:46.460
If you installed a legally 
gray-zone patch available

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.310
on the Internet to expand its functionality,

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:53.030
your device was effectively taken over.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.490
Without your knowledge.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:56.940
A back-door app...

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.070
Logos was using it to find 
more potential patsies?

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.970
Then whoever developed 
and distributed Liko was...

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:05.950
Probably Logos, or rather, Mythos.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.960
Yes, the likelihood is high.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:13.070
Also, Liko has morphed into a 
completely different program:

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:16.430
Benu, a program for control 
as well as surveillance.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:19.280
Because concealing its existence 
is no longer necessary?

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:23.460
It's taken over more than seventy 
percent of civilian computers.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.430
Do you think Mythos is a minor, after all?

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:26.440
They need disciplining.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:27.290
What?

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:28.520
Disciplining?

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:34.330
For us adults to uphold common decency, 
we need to discipline naughty children!

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:44.660
<i>In response to an increase in heinous crimes,</i>

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:49.040
<i>a new movement is picking up steam in police 
and security forces around the world.</i>

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:55.050
<i>This is the story of the services 
performed by ACTIVE in Japan.</i>

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.910
<b>File 12: For Whom Does Order Exist?</b>

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:11.260
<b>Baths</b>

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.830
With the impure as his father and mother,

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:23.050
<b>Tomohisa — Current Status: Missing   

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:23.830
how can the infant hope to become a human?

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.320
<b>Delete File and All Related Data</b>

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:25.680
<b>All data pertaining to the selected individual will be deleted, 
including backup data. Do you want to proceed? 
Delete</b>

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:28.410
Tonight, a child of God will be born...

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:33.270
All right, next...

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.730
Next?

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.950
How did this happen?

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.980
Weren't our emergency measures ironclad?!

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:43.510
Your Finance Ministry skimped on the security 
allocation to keep the opposition happy!

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:44.360
We didn't—

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.540
I said to save the blame game for later!

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:47.240
Prime Minister!

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:47.780
Yes?

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.580
Why do you have the Defense Ministry 
and the police with you?

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.170
At any rate, it's a saving grace that our lifeline

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.060
and communications infrastructure are still intact.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:04:00.220
But the fact that we can't even reboot the 
stock market without Mythos's permission...

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:01.270
Chief Cabinet Secretary...

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:02.260
Y-Yes, sir?

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.670
The US has informed us that their 
carrier strike group is en route.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.790
We've denied the terrorist attack by Logos,

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:09.350
but it's only a matter of time...

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:12.470
Chairman Sasaki of the finance alliance 
and Diet member Ishikawa from

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.190
the local Diet caucus request an audience.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.230
I don't have time for that right now!

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.710
We can barely travel or do 
anything with our money,

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:20.850
and the TV and radio are still off-line.

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:23.320
Yet there's no explanation from the government!

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:27.700
This goes far beyond simple lack of 
accountability on their part!

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.950
This is your chance to stand 
with us, the opposition,

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.910
and return power to the hands of the people!

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:40.760
Sorry to make you all stay overnight.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.210
Well, it's a state of emergency.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:46.570
All the other divisions seem to be barely 
keeping up with safeguarding their own.

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:47.700
It's the least we can do.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.680
Thank God the supermarket's still open.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.980
Should we go buy a change of clothes later?

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.440
Boss?

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.420
I thought you went to headquarters with Sena...

00:04:58.420 --> 00:04:59.650
Did you forget something?

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:02.470
Um, I'm her sister.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:04.250
Oh, Hinata-san.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:05.900
Did you need something from our boss?

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.370
Well, there's this thing on my laptop.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:16.000
It used to be so fun...

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.810
I hope this will be our final conversation.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.460
My parents should be in Poland.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.240
I can't get in touch with them.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:27.930
Anyway, about Mythos's real name and location...

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.120
Oh, come on!

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.870
If we could at least reach his parents...

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.380
It'll take time. They're overseas.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:35.890
Rin...

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:38.740
Oh, is something wrong, Inagi-kun?

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.650
There was an inter-partisan meeting.

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:42.250
Anyway, have you heard?

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:42.980
Heard what?

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:46.450
It appears the prime minister 
has made a major decision.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:49.900
The SAT has issued orders to the USDF.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.530
What's going on?

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:54.910
They have shoot-to-kill orders for Mythos, 
Logos's self-proclaimed leader,

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:58.310
as a terrorist jeopardizing national security.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:05:59.090
Shoot to kill?

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.500
A minor?

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.850
Should Mythos be killed,

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:10.550
<b>Administrator Access Rights 

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:05.370
administrator access goes to the next 
in line, the chief cabinet secretary.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:09.780
Given the security risks, I guess they're 
between a rock and a hard place.

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:12.530
That Mythos is a minor will be buried,

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:15.630
in accordance with the Specified 
Secrets Protection Bill.

00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:16.590
Boss?

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.210
If that's the law and there's a directive...

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:21.360
What's going on here?

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:22.680
Director General...

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:26.070
Inagi-sensei, someone from the 
Diet office is looking for you.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.940
Oh, thank you for letting me know.

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.770
Director General Kaidou, about what 
we were discussing just now—

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:31.460
Chief,

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.620
Mythos has made contact.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:38.670
That's why I came back here from 
the prime minister's residence.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:39.920
What does he want?

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.580
To talk to Bird, AKA Hachijou.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:43.450
Huh?!

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:44.340
Did they run a trace?

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:46.650
He routed the request through overseas servers,

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:48.170
so it'll be hard to trace.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:51.700
We also received word from 
Funasaka-san's Kichijouji group.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:54.010
Something from Logos was on Hinata-san's laptop.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.220
Got it.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:58.510
Okay, I'm putting it up.

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:02.290
<i>The system you are using is under Logos control.</i>

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:04.870
<i>Please be aware that you will not be able</i>

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:07.690
<i>to perform any tasks not authorized by Logos...</i>

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:11.410
Isn't this Benu, the hijacked version of Liko?

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.440
That's not the only thing, though.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:15.370
A notice from Liko-chan is still showing up.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:17.580
What did you ask Liko-chan to do?

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:21.560
I just asked her to collect data for my paper...

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.290
Something isn't right.

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:28.620
Well, Bird messed around with 
Hinata-san's laptop, right?

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:29.530
It's possible that

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:34.260
this laptop escaped the Logos takeover
due to its being used for the holograms.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:35.610
A blind spot?

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:39.980
<b>Everything Portal</b>

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:39.980
<b>Fruit of Tragedy</b>

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:39.980
But I doubt the data has much to do with Logos.

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:44.150
<b>National Public Safety Commission 
Police Headquarters</b>

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:46.110
Mythos?

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:48.670
Very well.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:50.280
Hello?

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:54.260
Hi. I guess your real name is Hachijou Tomoki?

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.280
Why the sudden call?

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.780
It's to come up with the ultimate plan.

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:02.330
Will that be fun?

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:03.730
It will.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:06.170
I'm wondering if our past MO is for the best.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:07.770
Up to now,

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:11.140
was there anyone with whom you 
felt you could talk as equals?

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.470
I can have you released right now.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.130
In return...

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.220
You want to rebuild society?

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:17.010
Yes.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.180
Let's split admin rights to do that.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:22.290
One, seven, four, two, eight,

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:24.690
nine, two, zero, seven, five,

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:24.690
What's going on?

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:27.650
three, three, four, two, three,

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:30.150
nine, eight, seven, two, zero.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.760
I understand how you feel.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:34.750
Well, later, then.

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:37.520
All right, I'll let the government know.

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:40.990
That was a Vernam cipher, right?

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:41.830
Well done.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:45.560
Does Mythos intend to initiate a 
deal using that information?

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:48.410
Now that he even controls everyone's savings,

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:50.730
I doubt the government can refuse.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:53.170
This wasn't part of the original plan, was it?

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.890
There's no need to take such a roundabout route.

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:58.760
Right. I wasn't expecting this, personally.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.520
This is a surprise!

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:05.230
I guess I need to return a surprise in kind.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:16.200
<b>Shinjuku Station</b>

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:07.540
Mythos must have used

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:11.010
the cipher to tell Hachijou the 
admin-access password.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:12.690
If the access is shared,

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:16.200
even if one's taken out, the other can retaliate.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.720
Can you decrypt it?

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.630
Not without knowing the random number key.

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.460
Sena-kun, where's the command vehicle?

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:23.160
It's been repaired. It's back in Kichijouji.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:30.540
<b>Railway Usage Permissions</b>

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:28.270
But the railways have been restricted, 
so we can only use air routes.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:30.540
<b>Denied</b>

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:29.940
Um, boss...

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:30.540
Yes?

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.240
About the prime minister...

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:35.170
Oh, the director general said 
they just wanted his advice.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:39.080
Our tasks remain confirming Mythos's 
identity and bringing him in.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:37.210
Yes.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.260
But how do we figure out who he is?

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.590
It's Funasaka-san!

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:44.770
They found out who Mythos is.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:45.390
What?!

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:46.020
Huh?

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.940
Please tell us more!

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.470
This is Yamabuki.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:54.360
Apparently, Hinata-san's Liko was gathering data.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:54.910
Yes, I understand.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.010
They're locating his hiding place now.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:56.820
Funasaka-san?

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:00.780
Looks like he bailed from this hideout.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.590
Is there another safe house,

00:10:02.590 --> 00:10:03.990
or is he here somewhere?

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:05.170
Wait a minute.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:07.710
He's evidently made contact 
asking the government to negotiate.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:17.520
Well?

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:20.010
Have you prepared a flight for me yet?

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:22.680
We still need a little more time for fueling.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:26.980
We also want air-traffic control 
systems to be fully restored.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.740
Are you trying to buy time?

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:30.630
You'd better not try to pull anything.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.550
I've made appropriate countermeasures.

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:34.020
I see!

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:35.850
Our guess would be

00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:39.490
the missiles you used back in the poker incident.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.380
Hey, minor. Been a while.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:45.900
It's me! Remember?

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:47.940
Sorry I barged in like that back then.

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:49.560
I was kind of on-edge.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:50.620
You!

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.010
I thought you might be the guy from the bath...

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:56.330
Well, I had kinda guessed 
based on the route you used,

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:57.440
but anyway...

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:01.060
Mythos, your game ends here!

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:02.380
Impossible!

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:04.190
Even if you figured out who I am,

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:05.620
how did you locate that ship?

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:08.890
You told Hachijou lots of things, didn't you?

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:09.640
Huh?

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:13.230
Hachijou sold you out with regard 
to your planned escape route.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:16.180
He brokered a deal before you did.

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:17.670
Huh? What do you—

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:19.780
You've been betrayed.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.040
Lies!

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:23.180
That's impossible, after I've come this far!

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:25.210
He's Bird!

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.740
He'd never...

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.290
You're smart, so I'll assume you 
know what happens next.

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:32.500
Then, I'll go ahead with the protocol.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.470
This is the police!

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:35.960
Power down the Willwear, and you'll—

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:38.070
Are you sure you want to go that route?

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:40.160
I'll blow up all the buildings around here.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:41.050
Fire.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:43.390
Huh?

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:44.220
Damn it!

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:47.240
You're not getting away!

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:49.020
You specifically targeted this location!

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:51.730
Yeah, we're smart, too.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:56.150
We jammed all the networks and 
analog lines we could think of.

00:11:56.490 --> 00:11:59.410
That Wear of yours isn't linked to anything now.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:01.610
In other words, it's a standalone unit!

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:02.310
Huh?

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:05.290
You're completely isolated. Get it?

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:06.480
Isolated?

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:08.580
Isolated?

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:12.900
After being expelled from the system 
known as Japan, I'm isolated now?

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:14.530
How ironic.

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:16.680
I won't let that happen!

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:21.080
I'll get out of here, and exercise 
system-admin privileges.

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:23.590
And when I do, the one enslaved

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:25.250
will be you.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.250
Sitrep?

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:39.250
Not good.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.540
Oscar II's pinned him down,

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:44.620
but Mythos's Wear has a higher MTQ,

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:46.780
so bringing him in won't be easy.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:51.630
If Mythos leaves the area where Oscar III and 
Kyoukai-san are jamming communications,

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:53.660
he may exercise admin privileges

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.460
and take out our system.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.710
Is it really that cult leader who's Mythos?

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.410
Yes, there's no question.

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:03.600
Um, I was living overseas when it all happened,

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:05.330
so I don't really know the details...

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:07.080
About the Fruit of Tragedy?

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:08.050
Right.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.890
It's nothing good.

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:13.550
A cult committed mass suicide,

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.640
taking many innocent lives.

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:20.710
The cult's leader was a boy of only five

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:23.360
whose parents instigated the mass suicide.

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:25.820
And that boy is Mythos, from Logos?

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.950
If I can just get out of the jamming area...

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.560
Not gonna happen!

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:38.120
Don't be stupid! My Wear is more powerful!

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.400
So, that Willwear

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:43.170
is the one being developed 
for military use in the EU.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:45.230
But our pilots have more training!

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:47.970
Its specs so surpass ours, 
that may not make a difference.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.140
Crap!

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:06.350
Oscar I, set Elf Sigma unit.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:08.850
Chief,

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.660
Mythos may cause our system to shut down.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.470
I need you to buy time.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:17.550
Government agencies and 
the Willwear Association

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:19.490
are jointly trying to access Orochi.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:22.420
Oh, they're going to reset the password?

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:24.470
Yes, so in the meantime,

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:27.380
we need Mythos to stay within the jamming area.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.840
Use analog radio to communicate.

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:32.970
Bastard, get off your high horse!

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.350
You're just scum who has a few years on me.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.580
Shut up!

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:44.440
Don't poke fun at adults—

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:45.820
What are you doing?!

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.660
You let him escape the jamming area!

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:53.180
I can now exercise admin privileges again.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:53.950
I won't let you!

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.250
Wh-What?

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:02.190
Crap!

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:03.000
He's getting away!

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.000
Oscar VI is landing a kick!

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:10.260
Oops...

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:12.640
There!

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.020
I see...

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:18.350
You absolutely insist on fighting me, then?

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:24.080
How much longer until we regain admin access?

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:27.360
Unfortunately, there are 
many layers of protection.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:30.700
Not even Unit 8 can last forever against him.

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.100
Defense Minister...

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:32.660
Sir?

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:35.760
I still can't find it.

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.030
Looks like he used his admin privileges

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:40.570
to delete his family registry 
and a lot of other info.

00:15:40.570 --> 00:15:41.960
Even information about his family?

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:42.580
Yes.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:48.800
So we only have the data Hinata 
asked Liko-chan to get...

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:51.620
He attracted unwanted 
attention wherever he went,

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:53.850
so he didn't attend elementary school.

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:56.890
I wonder if he's self-funding through investment.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:16:00.060
I see... He had a little sister.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:05.160
Could you refrain from interfering further?

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:07.190
It's not as if I want to hurt anyone.

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:09.580
I'm just trying to rule

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:11.630
the country that expelled me.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:13.660
Your lives will not be changed.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.430
Of course they'd be changed!

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:17.540
This isn't a dictatorship!

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.620
See some sense, will you?

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.420
You're the ones who made me see sense.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:25.080
Police did nothing. You have no right to talk!

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:29.300
Based on Liko's data, he changed 
his surname several times.

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:33.260
His sister moved overseas to 
escape negative publicity,

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:36.010
but he wasn't allowed to follow her.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:36.840
Why not?

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.150
Some of his cultists were scattered overseas,

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:41.560
so it was deemed too dangerous to let him go.

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:45.410
I see. So all this time, he's been 
trapped in Japanese society.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:46.520
However...

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:48.180
It's no use.

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:50.630
Unit 8's gear is no match for mine.

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:51.990
Listen, Mythos...

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:54.570
We're partners living in the same country.

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.530
Don't you think we should observe the rules?

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.050
That is meaningless talk.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:00.330
I need no partners.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:04.100
Well... It's about time to get rid of you all.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.290
You're lying.

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:08.750
You wanted Hachijou, AKA Bird, 
to be your partner.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.550
You wanted someone to talk to. Am I wrong?

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:15.830
I also thought, at first, that I 
didn't need any partners,

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:17.080
so I understand...

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:19.430
You want friends, don't you?

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:21.310
Don't sound so pleased with yourself.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:23.310
A-Akatsuki Revised, activate!

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:27.160
Take that, and that, and that, and that, and that—

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:29.650
A fiasco!

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:32.770
Not this way!

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:36.490
Crap, the jamming's down!

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:38.450
We didn't plan for this!

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:42.490
You cannot overpower me, either.

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:45.960
Chief, what's the status on 
the password-reset effort?!

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:48.420
Still waiting to hear. Can't you 
manage to keep him there?

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:51.090
I've won—

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:57.710
These markers are USDF's...

00:17:57.710 --> 00:17:58.760
...special ops.

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:01.250
Slasher platoons, this is 01.

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:03.470
Report positions, over.

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:04.650
This is 21.

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:06.670
All men are in firing position, over.

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:08.540
Unit 8,

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:11.430
USDF now has jurisdiction in this operation.

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:12.520
Retreat.

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:15.030
We haven't received any such order.

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:18.450
Until we do, abandoning our directive 
to take the target into custody

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.990
would be a violation of our duty.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.950
Then we'll just carry out our directive.

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:25.630
Command vehicle, what should we do?

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:28.410
The brass is in disarray, and we can't get through.

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:30.140
I suggest a temporary retreat.

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:31.710
No, we're staying.

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:35.630
If we just stand by and watch him die,

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:37.970
we can't call ourselves cops!

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:41.620
Um, they're going to attack for real.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.640
I really don't want to die.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.970
Right?

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:47.850
So, Mythos, it's time to power down your Wear!

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:50.430
As someone who shared the bath with you,

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:52.880
I don't want to see you die!

00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:55.130
Stop projecting your feelings on—

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:57.860
You had good memories there, didn't you?

00:18:57.860 --> 00:18:59.070
It's none of your business!

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:00.790
Cut the crap already!

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:03.110
To be honest, I want to beat 
you up before arresting—

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:06.060
If you insist on obstructing our operation,

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:07.790
we will neutralize you, as per protocol.

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:10.700
We're acting per protocol here, too.

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:13.000
Hey! Is death your ultimate goal?!

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:15.460
I have Bird.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:17.210
As long as he's alive, it doesn't matter.

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:19.630
You're still holding on to that?!

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:18.690
<b>Communications Restored</b>

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:19.840
<b>You Have Mail</b>

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:20.800
<b>Extracting</b>

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:21.070
A message from Bird?

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:22.440
<i>Hi, Mythos.</i>

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:24.400
<i>I have been utterly disappointed by</i>

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:26.610
<i>your need for partners.</i>

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:28.760
<i>We will never see each other again.</i>

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:30.110
<i>Goodbye.</i>

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:37.780
I...

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:39.440
I...

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:42.590
Boss, can I use that intel now?

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:43.520
That?

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:45.840
Okay, I grant permission.

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:51.360
Um, we'd like Tomohisa-san, 
AKA Mythos-san, to hear something.

00:19:51.980 --> 00:19:54.630
Your sister is probably alive.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:55.650
Huh?

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:58.900
We found evidence among the 
information Liko collected.

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:01.650
She seems to have changed citizenships and such.

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:06.240
But if a reunion is possible, we 
recommend not throwing your life away.

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:39.750
Well, that was a close call the other day, huh?

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:43.200
If the government hadn't managed to

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:45.900
reset the password before he surrendered...

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:49.220
The USDF might have shot him.

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:56.270
<i>Liko's totally back!</i>

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:58.360
Oh, she's really back!

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:02.440
Oh, Liko-chan's okay now?

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:06.150
Yeah, Mythos was pretty straightforward 
in his testimony about fixing her.

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:08.040
Can we really trust him?

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:08.910
Why not?

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:13.090
From his point of view, Liko was 
meant to be one-time use,

00:21:13.090 --> 00:21:15.440
but she gave him the 
information he most wanted.

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:18.130
He's no longer alone.

00:21:18.350 --> 00:21:22.300
If this has become a symbol of hope for Mythos,

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:23.840
I suppose he wouldn't booby trap it.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:25.980
Actually, about Hachijou...

00:21:25.980 --> 00:21:28.710
He went off somewhere after 
passing through Singapore?

00:21:28.710 --> 00:21:31.310
Yeah. What do we do about him now?

00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:35.680
His release was an extra-legal measure, 
so we can't touch him now.

00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:38.230
But if he ever comes back, 
I'll knock him out cold!

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:41.070
That's how I choose to think of it.

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:42.690
We have plenty of cases to go around.

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:44.570
We shouldn't get too hung up on him.

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:45.560
Right.

00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:47.470
So, about the wrap party for our good work...

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:50.030
I found a restaurant. It's a Chinese place.

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:51.490
All right, then!

00:21:51.860 --> 00:21:53.200
Tonight, for once, let's...

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:54.080
...party 'til dawn?

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:56.500
I may come along, for once.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:58.460
I guess I can't say no.

00:21:59.590 --> 00:22:02.420
Other than Kazari, the minor, 
the rest of us can party 'til dawn.

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:04.880
No, I'll take the last train home.

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:05.970
Huh?

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:08.430
I have to take out the 
non-combustibles in the morning.

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:10.120
I... I see.

00:22:10.120 --> 00:22:13.040
I'm not convinced, but whatever.

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:14.890
Let's party!

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:16.030
Yeah!

00:22:16.030 --> 00:22:19.030
Oh, by the way, I just turned twenty.

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:20.450
Huh?

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:21.810
Kazari-kun,

00:22:21.810 --> 00:22:24.110
why didn't you report such an important event?

00:22:24.310 --> 00:22:27.570
Okay, we'll be celebrating 
Asami's birthday today, too.

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:28.530
Huh?

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:30.530
Er... Are you all okay with that?

00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:31.650
Yeah!

00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:33.280
Happy Birthday!
